     3,
     "\r<br>On Mon, 2021-09-13 at 06:08 -0700, Uma Mahi wrote:\r<br>&gt; Hi INLA group members, \r<br>&gt; I am running a spatio temporal model considering database from\r<br>&gt; duration Jan 2013 to Dec 2018 (72 months) with 502 areas.\r<br>&gt; I am trying to plot monthly temporal pattern (Observed and predicted\r<br>&gt; incidence rate ratio) which is calculated as follows\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; SMR &lt;-\r<br>&gt; apply(matrix(data$O,S,T,byrow=F),2,sum)/apply(matrix(data$E,S,T,byrow=\r<br>&gt; F),2,sum)\r<br>&gt; temporal &lt;-\r<br>&gt; unlist(lapply(main_Model2$marginals.lincomb.derived[(S+2):(1+S+T)],\r<br>&gt; function(x) inla.emarginal(exp,x)))\r<br>&gt; aux &lt;- lapply(main_Model2$marginals.lincomb.derived[(S+2):(1+S+T)],\r<br>&gt; function(x) inla.tmarginal(exp,x))\r<br>&gt; q1 &lt;- unlist(lapply(aux, function(x) inla.qmarginal(0.025,x)))\r<br>&gt; q2 &lt;- unlist(lapply(aux, function(x) inla.qmarginal(0.975,x)))\r<br>&gt; I would like to know whether the predicted emarginals from\r<br>&gt; “marginals.lincomb.derived” for the 72 months are based on all the 502\r<br>&gt; spatial areas.\r<br>&gt;  \r<br>"
