   "subject": "Re: [r-inla] predicted temporal pattern calculation",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "the easiest way to check this is to run with\r<br>\r<br>control.inla=list(strategy=&quot;gaussian&quot;, int.strategy=&quot;eb&quot;)\r<br>\r<br>and then the mean&#39;s should match. compare the means of the lincomb&#39;s\r<br>with the corresponding mean of the temporal patterns etc... \r<br>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "\r<br>\r<br>On Tue, 2021-09-14 at 10:59 +0530, Uma Mahi wrote:\r<br>&gt; Hi Rue\r<br>&gt; I am very thankful for your timely response as it helps us.\r<br>&gt; I have few clarifications based on your response “How these linear\r<br>&gt; combinations defined?”\r<br>&gt; When running the model, I have used the linear combinations which is\r<br>&gt; given below:\r<br>&gt;  \r<br>&gt; ## Posterior distribution of the global intercept ##\r<br>&gt;  \r<br>&gt; lc1 = inla.make.lincomb(Predictor = rep(1/(S*T),S*T))\r<br>&gt; names(lc1) &lt;- &quot;intercept&quot;\r<br>&gt;  \r<br>&gt;  \r<br>&gt; ## Posterior distribution of the spatial pattern ##\r<br>&gt;  \r<br>&gt; M1 &lt;- matrix(-1/(S*T),S,S*T)\r<br>&gt; for (i in 1:S) {\r<br>&gt;   M1[i,seq(0,S*(T-1),by=S)+i] &lt;- 1/(S*T)*(S-1)\r<br>&gt; }\r<br>&gt; lc2 = inla.make.lincombs(Predictor = M1)\r<br>&gt; names(lc2) &lt;- paste(&quot;spatial.&quot;,as.character(seq(1:S)),sep=&quot;&quot;)\r<br>&gt;  \r<br>&gt;  \r<br>&gt; ## Posterior distribution of the temporal pattern ##\r<br>&gt;  \r<br>&gt; M2 &lt;- matrix(-1/(S*T),T,S*T)\r<br>&gt; for (i in 1:T) {\r<br>&gt;   M2[i,seq(1,S)+S*(i-1)] &lt;- 1/(S*T)*(T-1)\r<br>&gt; }\r<br>&gt; lc3 = inla.make.lincombs(Predictor = M2)\r<br>&gt; names(lc3) &lt;- paste(&quot;temporal.&quot;,as.character(seq(1:T)),sep=&quot;&quot;)\r<br>&gt;  \r<br>&gt;  \r<br>&gt; ## Posterior distribution of the spatio-temporal pattern ##\r<br>&gt;  \r<br>&gt; M3 &lt;- matrix(1/(S*T),S*T,S*T)\r<br>&gt; k=1\r<br>&gt; for (j in 1:T) {\r<br>&gt;   for (i in 1:S) {\r<br>&gt;     M3[k,seq(0,S*(T-1),by=S)+i] &lt;- 1/(S*T)*(1-S)\r<br>&gt;     M3[k,seq(1,S)+S*(j-1)] &lt;- 1/(S*T)*(1-T)\r<br>&gt;     M3[k,k] &lt;- (S*T-S-T+1)/(S*T)\r<br>&gt;     k=k+1\r<br>&gt;   }\r<br>&gt; }\r<br>&gt; lc4 = inla.make.lincombs(Predictor = M3)\r<br>&gt; names(lc4) &lt;-\r<br>&gt; paste(&quot;spatio.temporal.&quot;,as.character(seq(1:(S*T))),sep=&quot;&quot;)\r<br>&gt;  \r<br>&gt; <a href=\"http://all.lc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://all.lc&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792439273084000&amp;usg=AOvVaw38VhXkuBLvfnJyJkrAky9N\">all.lc</a>&lt;- c(lc1,lc2,lc3,lc4)\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; My questions are:\r<br>&gt;  \r<br>&gt; (1)  Whether the r-codes for the posterior-distribution of the\r<br>&gt; temporal pattern would result in predictions for 72 months? Please\r<br>&gt; correct me if I am wrong.\r<br>&gt;  \r<br>&gt; (2)  In the “marginal.lincomb.derived” estimates for each month I have\r<br>&gt; only 35 rows. I would like to know what this number “35” refers to? Is\r<br>&gt; it the no. of samples randomly generated from the posterior\r<br>&gt; distribution or the rows for each time point         corresponding to\r<br>&gt; the no. of blocks, if so, which was found to be less than the total\r<br>&gt; no. of blocks (502) in my data set? Kindly clarify.\r<br>&gt;  \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Thanks and Regards\r<br>&gt; R.Uma Maheswari\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; On Tue, Sep 14, 2021 at 1:02 AM Helpdesk &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">he...@r-inla.org</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt; &gt; \r<br>&gt; &gt; that would depend on how these linear combinations are defined,\r<br>&gt; &gt; which\r<br>&gt; &gt; is\r<br>&gt; &gt; not given.\r<br>&gt; &gt; \r<br>&gt; &gt; On Mon, 2021-09-13 at 06:08 -0700, Uma Mahi wrote:\r<br>&gt; &gt; &gt; Hi INLA group members, \r<br>&gt; &gt; &gt; I am running a spatio temporal model considering database from\r<br>&gt; &gt; &gt; duration Jan 2013 to Dec 2018 (72 months) with 502 areas.\r<br>&gt; &gt; &gt; I am trying to plot monthly temporal pattern (Observed and\r<br>&gt; &gt; &gt; predicted\r<br>&gt; &gt; &gt; incidence rate ratio) which is calculated as follows\r<br>&gt; &gt; &gt; \r<br>&gt; &gt; &gt; SMR &lt;-\r<br>&gt; &gt; &gt; \r<br>&gt; &gt; apply(matrix(data$O,S,T,byrow=F),2,sum)/apply(matrix(data$E,S,T,byro\r<br>&gt; &gt; w=\r<br>&gt; &gt; \r<br>&gt; &gt; &gt; F),2,sum)\r<br>&gt; &gt; &gt; temporal &lt;-\r<br>&gt; &gt; &gt; unlist(lapply(main_Model2$marginals.lincomb.derived[(S+2):(1+S+T)]\r<br>&gt; &gt; &gt; ,\r<br>&gt; &gt; &gt; function(x) inla.emarginal(exp,x)))\r<br>&gt; &gt; &gt; aux &lt;-\r<br>&gt; &gt; &gt; lapply(main_Model2$marginals.lincomb.derived[(S+2):(1+S+T)],\r<br>&gt; &gt; &gt; function(x) inla.tmarginal(exp,x))\r<br>&gt; &gt; &gt; q1 &lt;- unlist(lapply(aux, function(x) inla.qmarginal(0.025,x)))\r<br>&gt; &gt; &gt; q2 &lt;- unlist(lapply(aux, function(x) inla.qmarginal(0.975,x)))\r<br>&gt; &gt; &gt; I would like to know whether the predicted emarginals from\r<br>&gt; &gt; &gt; “marginals.lincomb.derived” for the 72 months are based on all the\r<br>&gt; &gt; 502\r<br>&gt; &gt; &gt; spatial areas.\r<br>&gt; &gt; &gt;  \r<br>&gt; &gt; &gt; -- \r<br>&gt; &gt; &gt; You received this message because you are subscribed to the Google\r<br>&gt; &gt; &gt; Groups &quot;R-inla discussion group&quot; group.\r<br>&gt; &gt; &gt; To unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it,\r<br>&gt; &gt; send\r<br>&gt; &gt; &gt; an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">r-inla-discussion...@googlegroups.com</a>.\r<br>&gt; &gt; &gt; To view this discussion on the web, visit\r<br>&gt; &gt; &gt; \r<br>&gt; &gt; <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/r-inla-discussion-group/caf10896-ae18-4e1f-a657-07d7e47cf523n%40googlegroups.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/r-inla-discussion-group/caf10896-ae18-4e1f-a657-07d7e47cf523n%2540googlegroups.com&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792439273084000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0rsBZsREcXKzf7pyMO-oxe\">https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/r-inla-discussion-group/caf10896-ae18-4e1f-a657-07d7e47cf523n%40googlegroups.com</a>\r<br>&gt; &gt; &gt; .\r<br>&gt; &gt; \r<br>\r<br>-- \r<br>Håvard Rue\r<br><a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">he...@r-inla.org</a>\r<br>\r<br>"
